; Bundle-dispatch stress — the bundle arm of a dispatch-throughput comparison
; after the webgpu-samples `animometer` sample. 60 hash-placed triangles, each
; drawn by its own `(render-bundle …)` with its own uniform buffer and bind
; group (the triangle index rides in the uniform), executed as 4 passes × 15
; bundles. Upstream measures per-frame JS encoding cost, which a pre-recorded
; payload does not have; this file stresses the per-frame path pngine does
; run — bytecode walk → command buffer → JS application — at 60 bundle
; executions each carrying a bind-group switch.
;
; Sizing: `:execute-bundles` takes at most 16 bundles per pass, hence the
; four passes; N=60 also stays under the bind-group and buffer limits with
; headroom. The first pass writes timestamps 0/1 and the last 2/3 (a count-4
; query set; total = ts3 − ts0), resolved and copied to a MAP_READ buffer for
; the host's onQueryResult. Companion: webgpu_stress_instanced.sjon draws the
; same 60 triangles as one instanced draw. Measured on M-series Metal / Chrome
; at DPR 2 (65.536 µs timestamp steps), both arms run display-limited (~118
; fps); GPU time ~262 µs for the bundle arm (at an earlier 256-bundle,
; 16-pass prototype) vs ~66 µs instanced — dispatch overhead is measurable
; but far from the frame budget. Native `--frame`: bundles and queries are
; no-ops, so it shows only the clear.

(shader-module :name code :code """
struct Info { v : vec4f }
@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> info : Info;

fn hash(n: u32) -> f32 {
  var x = n;
  x = ((x >> 16u) ^ x) * 0x45d9f3bu;
  x = ((x >> 16u) ^ x) * 0x45d9f3bu;
  x = (x >> 16u) ^ x;
  return f32(x) / f32(0xffffffffu);
}

struct VSOut {
  @builtin(position) pos : vec4f,
  @location(0) color : vec3f,
}

@vertex
fn vs(@builtin(vertex_index) vi : u32) -> VSOut {
  let i = u32(info.v.x);
  let c = vec2f(hash(i * 3u + 1u), hash(i * 3u + 2u)) * 1.9 - 0.95;
  let s = 0.03;
  var corners = array<vec2f, 3>(vec2f(0.0, s), vec2f(-s, -s), vec2f(s, -s));
  var out : VSOut;
  out.pos = vec4f(c + corners[vi], 0.0, 1.0);
  let hue = hash(i * 3u) * 6.2831853;
  out.color = 0.55 + 0.45 * vec3f(cos(hue), cos(hue - 2.0944), cos(hue + 2.0944));
  return out;
}

@fragment
fn fs(@location(0) color : vec3f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
  return vec4f(color, 1.0);
}
""")

(render-pipeline :name pipe
  :layout auto
  (vertex :module code :entry vs)
  (fragment :module code :entry fs
    (target :format preferred-canvas-format))
  (primitive :topology triangle-list))

(query-set :name tsQS :type timestamp :count 4)
(buffer :name resolveBuf :size 32 :usage [query-resolve copy-src])
(buffer :name readbackBuf :size 32 :usage [map-read copy-dst])

